{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty","kind":"remark","title":"Mathematical novelty of the genus-saturation force-carrier derivation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-force-carrier-bring-uniqueness"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-force-carrier-bring-uniqueness","text":"force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty\"></a><p>The Diophantine constraint <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m-1)(n-1)=2g</code> enforces genus-saturation on the symplectic homology of Bring's surface. This algebraic geometry condition determines the force-carrier pair (knots with 9 and 10 crossings). It eliminates the need for auxiliary symmetry assumptions.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty.md","heading":"Remark","number":"16.5.9","page":"b/rem-force-carrier-bring-uniqueness-novelty","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
